  "solution": {
    "explanation": "Every palindrome has a centre, either a character or the gap between two. For each of the 2n-1 centres, expand left and right while the characters match, tracking the best span. Each expansion is O(n), giving O(n^2) time and O(1) extra space. Cubic brute force over all substrings is too slow on 1000-character inputs.",
    "code": "class Solution:\n    def longestPalindrome(self, s: str) -> str:\n        best = (0, 0)\n        n = len(s)\n        for c in range(2 * n - 1):\n            l, r = c // 2, c // 2 + c % 2\n            while l >= 0 and r < n and s[l] == s[r]:\n                l -= 1\n                r += 1\n            if r - l - 1 > best[1] - best[0]:\n                best = (l + 1, r)\n        return s[best[0]:best[1]]\n"
